# Two layer-1 fixes in dev-agents: a local dispatch lock and the catch-all role exit bug. 2026-09-12
#
# DISPATCH: ./scripts/dispatch.sh git@github.com:Arlencho/dev-agents.git wave-plans/dev-agents/2026-09-12-fleet-hygiene.plan --auto --retries 1
#
# Observed 2026-09-12 on macbook-pro-local:
#  (a) three concurrent dispatches shared one checkout at ~/dev/olympus-platform;
#      a producer reported its branch switched out from under it twice, and two
#      reviewer seats died in six seconds at the git stage (exit 128, no log file).
#  (b) a seat with role claude (the catch-all) finished its work, then the launcher
#      exit path printed: launch.sh: line 33: =/Users/arlenrios/dev/agent-runtime/roles/claude.md:
#      No such file or directory, and the seat was recorded as failed (exit 127),
#      so the dispatcher retried a finished task and never ran the next wave.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1 | devops | Two fixes in this repo, one branch, separate commits. FIX A, one local dispatch at a time. READ FIRST scripts/dispatch.sh and scripts/run-remote.sh, and confirm by reading that every localhost seat runs its git checkout and pull inside the same shared checkout under ~/dev/<repo>. Then add a per-repo lock to dispatch.sh for localhost workers only: before the first wave, acquire a lock file under the same state or log directory the script already uses, keyed by repo name; if another dispatch holds it, print one clear line naming the holder pid and the plan it is running, and either wait with a heartbeat line every 60 seconds until it frees or exit non-zero when a flag such as --no-wait is given; release the lock on every exit path including signals; document the flag in the usage text. Do not attempt the per-seat worktree redesign here; open a GitHub issue in this repo describing it (run-remote.sh should give each seat its own git worktree under a per-dispatch directory and remove it at seat exit) and reference the issue in the lock comment as the real fix. FIX B, the catch-all role exit. Reproduce first: in the sibling checkout at ../olympus-platform, run bash ~/dev/agent-runtime/launch.sh claude "print the word ok and stop" if that runtime exists on this machine, otherwise trace the shipped launcher from providers/claude/launch.sh and providers/lib.sh and the shipping step in scripts/run-remote.sh; find the code that builds a path from a roles directory and the role name, and fix it so a role with no charter file in roles/ (claude is the catch-all and has none) is handled explicitly rather than expanding to an empty variable executed as a command; decide with a one-line comment whether the catch-all should get a minimal roles/claude.md charter, and if yes add it, matching the shortest existing charter in form. VERIFY: bash -n on every touched script; run the reproduction again and paste the real exit code; run the existing test or lint target for scripts if make help lists one. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name in code comments, commit or PR text, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Open one PR. Do not merge. | fix/fleet-hygiene

2 | plan-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of branch fix/fleet-hygiene in dev-agents. No commits, no push, no edits, no labels; tmp writes only. Record the PR head SHA at start and at report. FIX A: prove the lock works by starting two dispatches of a trivial plan against the same repo in a tmp checkout, or by simulating the holder with a stale lock file, and show that the second one waits or exits per the flag; prove the lock is released on Ctrl-C and on a failed wave; confirm remote workers are unaffected; confirm the follow-up issue for per-seat worktrees exists and is referenced. FIX B: reproduce the original failure on the base commit if you can (role with no charter file), then confirm the fix on the branch returns the exit code of the agent run rather than 127, and that a role with a charter still gets it. Then: no long dash, no vendor name, no trailer. Post ONE comment on the PR whose first line reads CRITIC FLEET HYGIENE with SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX and line citations. | fix/fleet-hygiene
